    "question": {
      ":question/id": "564049b2-b3e7-5f60-b18f-bc063c2cf788",
      ":question/problem": "Determine the number of pivot columns of the matrix $D,$ given by\n\n$$\nD=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 2 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -12 & -6 & 0 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, we need to convert $D$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 2 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -12 & -6 & 0 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\quad {R}_{3} :={R}_{3}+(3){R}_{2} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 2 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $D$ has $3$ pivots, and therefore the number of pivot columns is $3.$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "e8e3fe2c-b4e8-5896-bb45-78e52c42c07c",
