    "question": {
      ":question/id": "eb507301-dca1-573e-84d7-83171cd2072c",
      ":question/problem": "Determine the number of pivot columns of the matrix $B,$ given by\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -3 & -1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -3 & -3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -3 & -1 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, we need to convert $B$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -3 & -1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -3 & -3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -3 & -1 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\quad {R}_{2} :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -3 & -1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -3 & -1 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\quad {R}_{3} :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -3 & -1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $B$ has $2$ pivots, and therefore the number of pivot columns is $2.$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "9accd259-06f8-5071-b3d8-65c18130b36c",
