    "question": {
      ":question/id": "d52d253e-3a12-5674-ba87-1c6fd9fae471",
      ":question/problem": "Determine the number of pivot columns of the matrix $A,$ given by\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 0 & 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 0 & -2 & -3 & 3 \\\\ 8 & 0 & -4 & -6 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, we need to convert $A$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 0 & 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 0 & -2 & -3 & 3 \\\\ 8 & 0 & -4 & -6 & -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\quad {R}_{2} :={R}_{2}+(1){R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 0 & 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 8 & 0 & -4 & -6 & -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\quad {R}_{3} :={R}_{3}+(2){R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 0 & 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $A$ has $2$ pivots, and therefore the number of pivot columns is $2.$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
